maxwell_3d: the split's front skips instance loop writes the back ignores (EDEN_NX2_LOOP_SKIP=1)

Core patch. Paths are the submodule's. Needs 0210 before it.

Source: zortos293/Lichii PR 178 (tibzejoker), head 95a227b710, and PR 179's switch,
GPL-3.0-or-later. Includes its later fixes: multi-method tracking (248450ef40), Replay (74fab5d4b0),
and index_buffer.first always sent (95a227b710: it marks the index buffer dirty).

draw.end inside an instance loop, and same-value vertex_buffer.first and .count, change nothing on
the back. Each is a ring entry and a method call on it. Lichii counted 520,000 and 390,000 a second
and 0 differences with EDEN_NX2_SPLIT_VERIFY, on a 13900K. The console's rates are not known.

Checked in our tree by reading: draw_mode changes only in DrawBegin, DrawArrayInstanced and
SetInlineIndexBuffer; vertex_buffer has no dirty table entry. A loop the front does not see only
means no skip.

Runs on the PS5: yes, with macros on the front (run61). Helps only if the back is the limit.
Hang: adds no wait. A wrong skip loses a draw. Pool memory: none.
Checked: PS5-target syntax compile. Not run. EDEN_NX2_SPLIT_VERIFY=1 compares registers, and a skip
leaves those equal: it finds a wrong value, not a lost draw. A lost draw shows on screen only.

